  "treeSemantics": "parentId is the breadcrumb parent, not the filesystem depth. level 0 is the corporate root, level 1 is a root-level page, level 2 is a detail or second-level page, level 3 is the family and bundle level. The proposed MAREA layer never exceeds level 3.",
  "authorizationSemantics": "Every authorization boolean records whether THIS MC-15 planning artefact authorizes the action. No MC-15 artefact authorizes publication, indexation, sitemap membership, commercial transaction or deployment, so every boolean is false, including for preserved corporate routes. A false value is not a statement that an existing corporate page is unpublished or de-indexed.",
  "preservationSemantics": "CORPORATE nodes reproduce the twenty-one current public route ids from the MC-15 data contract section 2.1 and preserve their breadcrumb parentage. The seven private admin route ids (section 2.2) and the three active legacy redirect ids (section 2.3) are preserved as root-level records (preservedPrivateRouteIds, preservedLegacyRedirects) rather than as public IA nodes, because they are not public navigation surfaces. Nothing here changes any route.",
